course: dictionary
lesson: 11594
title: Apothecary, an old word for a medicine-maker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An apothecary was a person who made and sold medicines long ago. Today we would call this person a pharmacist, or a chemist in the UK. Look for clues: «The sick girl took the powder the apothecary had mixed.» Mixed and powder tell you the apothecary made medicine.
explain: The word is old, so you will meet it mostly in history books and stories. Books about the Middle Ages, Tudor times and Victorian times use it. «The apothecary's shop was full of jars of herbs.» Jars and herbs are the clues that help you picture the shop.
explain: An apothecary also gave simple medical advice and treatment. «Mum took Tom to the apothecary with a sore throat, and he gave him a syrup and told him to rest.» Advice and treatment show that he helped sick people, not only sold things.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Does "the medicine-maker mixed the powder" still make sense in the sentence? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An apothecary was a person who made and sold medicines, and gave simple medical advice.
fact: Today this job is done by a pharmacist (UK: chemist; US: drugstore).
fact: In old times, an apothecary's shop had jars of herbs, powders and potions.
fact: In stories, an apothecary may sell cures, and sometimes poisons.
fact: «Apothecary» is a noun. Its plural is apothecaries.
exercise: «The apothecary mixed a green powder for the sick king.» What was the apothecary's job? | *To make and sell medicines | To teach children to swim | To sail ships | To build castles
exercise: «People went to the apothecary when they were ill.» What does apothecary mean? | *A person who made medicines and gave simple treatment | A person who built houses | A soldier who guarded a king | A teacher of music
exercise: Mia says the apothecary's shop sold cakes. Is she right? | No, it sold medicines, herbs and powders | *No, it sold medicines | Yes, cakes and sweets | Partly, it also sold bread
test: «The apothecary gave Tom a syrup for his cough and told him to rest.» What did the apothecary give Tom? | *A syrup for his cough | A bag of sweets | A letter from the king | A new pair of shoes
test: Today a pharmacist does the job that an old apothecary did. What is a pharmacist? | A person who grows apples | A person who mends roads | *A person who makes and sells medicines | A person who paints pictures
exam: In an old apothecary's shop, what would you most likely find? | Football boots | Bicycles | Surfboards | *Jars of herbs and powders
